From c1ca81616fe3fff642bc0efe26eed5fae2e56f78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:24:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep products consistent in Guided Story videos

- Split multi-view product collages into a single-view main photo plus
  labelled angles in the same single vision call; keep the collage only as
  a design reference (never a frame). Relabel, choose main, and generate a
  clean front shot from the sheet.
- Native-audio (Seedance) prompts now carry a [PRODUCT] block, labels and
  product-safe exclusions; Atlas Wan requests attach product photos, sheets
  and uploads; keyframes label the sheet as design-only.
- Product-only shots never start from a collage.
- Wearables: scenes list worn products, never show putting them on, and keep
  them worn in later scenes.
- Prompt clean-up: no stray hands, sentence-boundary trimming, sanitized
  backdrop direction, plain default wardrobe text, no on-screen text asks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0139LD6TNRqoUkkjABDyfiYJ
